# 2. Missing Data Handling

Missing values were identified using:

```python
df.isnull().sum()
```

An appropriate strategy was selected depending on the type and meaning of each column.

### Strategies Used

| Column Type              | Strategy     | Reason                                                         |
| ------------------------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Numerical                | Median       | Less affected by outliers                                      |
| Numerical                | Mean         | Used when values are normally distributed                      |
| Categorical              | Mode         | Most common category                                           |
| Date/Time                | Forward Fill | Useful for sequential records                                  |
| Critical/Invalid Records | Row Deletion | Used only when the missing record cannot be reliably recovered |

### Example

```python
# Numerical column
df["Age"] = df["Age"].fillna(df["Age"].median())

# Categorical column
df["Gender"] = df["Gender"].fillna(df["Gender"].mode()[0])
```

### Justification

Median imputation is preferred for numerical columns when the data contains outliers because the median is more robust than the mean.

Mode imputation is appropriate for categorical columns because it replaces missing values with the most frequently occurring category.

