# 5. Outlier Detection

Outliers were identified using the **IQR (Interquartile Range) method**.

The IQR method was applied to numerical columns.

```python
numeric_columns = df.select_dtypes(include=np.number).columns

for col in numeric_columns:
    Q1 = df[col].quantile(0.25)
    Q3 = df[col].quantile(0.75)

    IQR = Q3 - Q1

    lower_bound = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR
    upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR

    outliers = df[
        (df[col] < lower_bound) |
        (df[col] > upper_bound)
    ]

    print(col, "Outliers:", len(outliers))
```

### Outlier Treatment

Outliers were reviewed before deciding how to handle them.

Depending on the column, outliers were:

* Retained when they represented genuine observations
* Capped when extreme values could distort analysis
* Removed when they were clearly invalid

Genuine extreme values were not automatically deleted.

